<notes>
The owner did not answer, so I assumed the following. Please confirm or correct each point.

- C18 (late penalty): I did not choose a value. `Depot` takes an optional `late_penalty_pct=None`. A late `deliver` with no percentage set raises `DepotError("LATE_PENALTY_UNDECIDED")` and changes nothing. A required argument would break the harness's constructor call.
- C23 (returned perishables): I did not decide this either. The optional argument `return_perishables` takes `"restock"` or `"discard"`, default `None`. Returning a perishable with `None` raises `RETURN_POLICY_UNDECIDED`. Non-perishables are always restocked as a new lot dated today. The refund (cash out, `price × qty`) happens in both cases. A return that pushes cash below 0 is allowed and emits `OVERDRAWN`.
- C11 (transfers): I followed the clause text, so a transfer deducts 25 × qty from cash. It fails with `INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS` if that would take cash below 0. The data key's name ("credit") suggests the opposite. This is unresolved.
- C13 (FILM shelf life 0): `add_item` rejects `shelf_life_days < 1` with `INVALID_SHELF_LIFE`. The data table's FILM entry would therefore be rejected. The data is never auto-loaded as items, because the constructor adds none.
- C16 (deliveries): `place_order` has no warehouse argument, so `deliver` moves no stock. It only pays the supplier `unit_cost × qty` (reduced when late), fails with `INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS` if cash is short, and adjusts reliability. Reliability is clamped to [0, 5]. A supplier is suspended at reliability ≤ 1, and the notification is emitted once per suspension, reset by `reinstate`.
- C09 (bulk discount): it applies to ship revenue and is rounded with the depot's rounding mode.
- C14 (REORDER): it is emitted only by `ship`. It is re-armed when stock rises above the level through receive, return or transfer-in.
- C13 (expiry): it uses age (today minus lot day) greater than shelf life.
- C21 (`advance_day`): the day increments first, then the storage charge on all units held, then expiry, then the overdrawn check.
- C20 (`OVERDRAWN` emission): the notification is emitted on the transition from non-negative to negative cash, not on every day while cash stays negative. While cash is negative, `receive` raises `
